<section><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head rv"><span class="eyebrow">Available today</span><h2>Everything in the box now.</h2></div>
  <div class="grid g3">
    <div class="card rv"><h4>Intake and requirements <span class="badge b-live">Live</span></h4><ul class="tick"><li>Real Jira tickets, comments and workflow moves</li><li>PM agent with clarifying questions and auto-resume on reply</li><li>Contradiction detection with a stated default</li><li>Confluence pages as context</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card rv"><h4>Plan and build <span class="badge b-live">Live</span></h4><ul class="tick"><li>Project brief from your repository</li><li>EM plan and planning engineer</li><li>Dependency vetting before any package is added</li><li>Engineer that reads before it writes and checks its own work in a browser</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card rv"><h4>Review and test <span class="badge b-live">Live</span></h4><ul class="tick"><li>Independent reviewer that runs the tests itself</li><li>Tests re-run by the pipeline, not an agent's claim</li><li>Stacks: Node, Express and Postgres, Next.js and React</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card rv"><h4>QA in a real browser <span class="badge b-live">Live</span></h4><ul class="tick"><li>Blind test cases from the acceptance criteria</li><li>Every case in a fresh browser at three sizes</li><li>Results read from recorded runs, bugs with repro steps</li><li>Fix, replay with no model call, retest</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card rv"><h4>Evidence and delivery <span class="badge b-live">Live</span></h4><ul class="tick"><li>Screenshots and video at laptop, tablet and phone</li><li>Quality score against your product</li><li>Real GitHub pull request on a <code>showwork/</code> branch</li><li>Code review and PR-fix runs</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card rv"><h4>Control and platform <span class="badge b-live">Live</span></h4><ul class="tick"><li>Three human gates, bound to what was approved</li><li>Roles, approver alerts and a tamper-evident audit trail</li><li>Permission modes, budgets and live run messaging</li><li>MCP connectors and one-server self-hosting</li></ul></div>
  </div>
  <div class="grid g2" style="margin-top:1.3rem">
    <div class="card rv"><h4>Orchestrator <span class="badge b-live">Early access</span></h4><p>One orchestrator for the whole delivery, from the product manager to the code review, with the order enforced by guards in code.</p></div>
    <div class="card rv"><h4>Being validated now <span class="badge b-val">In validation</span></h4><ul class="tick"><li>Assertion-level QA: a case passes only when every assertion is proved</li><li>Failure kinds and a flake guard that reruns a failed case</li></ul></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

<section class="dark"><div class="wrap">
  <div class="section-head rv"><span class="eyebrow">Pipeline roadmap</span><h2>What ships next.</h2><p class="lede">Each step is built behind its own switch and measured on benchmark tickets before the next begins.</p></div>
  <div class="grid g3">
    <div class="card rv"><span class="badge b-val">Now</span><h3 style="margin-top:.7rem">Prove it, then default it</h3>
      <ul class="tick"><li>Assertion-level QA verification</li><li>Failure kinds and a flake guard for QA</li><li>Full orchestrator measured against the fixed pipeline on golden tickets, then made the default</li><li>Evidence per assertion and layout checks</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card rv"><span class="badge b-road">Next</span><h3 style="margin-top:.7rem">A bigger team on the pipeline</h3>
      <ul class="tick"><li><strong>Designer agent and design gate.</strong> Starts from a Figma link or your own CSS, drafts the screen at three sizes, and a person approves it (up to three rounds)</li><li><strong>Task splitting.</strong> The EM breaks large tickets into ordered tasks</li><li><strong>PM sign-off</strong> on QA results and screenshots before the patch gate</li><li>Researcher and clarifier agents, parallel review, asking a person mid-run</li></ul></div>
    <div class="card rv"><span class="badge b-road">Later</span><h3 style="margin-top:.7rem">Wider reach and stronger isolation</h3>
      <ul class="tick"><li><strong>Isolated environments.</strong> Each agent in its own copy, with results moved as patches</li><li><strong>Agents in containers</strong> behind a model proxy, with no secrets inside, for regulated and self-hosted teams</li><li>More stacks: MongoDB, monorepo folders, TypeScript and Vite templates</li><li>GitHub App and OAuth sign-in, more trackers and chat tools</li></ul></div>
  </div>
</div></section>

